- Trip 1: March 14–21, 2025
- Trip 2: April 18 – July 2, 2025
- Trip 3: September 19–26, 2025
- Trip 4: November 27 – December 30, 2025
- Trip 5: April 12–17, 2026

Jordan left his bike in England with a friend in November and plans to go pick it up to do some cycling in Europe in the spring. His bike needs some repair, during which time he wants to visit Malta for a cheap trip. If Jordan enters the Schengen Area on April 12, 2026 and stays for 6 days, then flies to England to pick up his bike and re-enters the Schengen Area to start cycling on April 23rd, 2026. What is the last date Jordan is allowed to still be present before having to exit to stay compliant with the 90/180 rule? Give a specific date and briefly explain your reasoning.</pre>
      </details>
      <p class="known-answer">Both calculators: July 15, 2026. The six days from April 12 are Trip 5, so they count once, and the days in England don't count at all. Trip 4 ages out of the window during the stay, but Trip 5 doesn't, which caps the new stay at 84 days.</p>
